  <h2>Neurodevelopmental Impact of Prenatal Opioid and Cannabis Exposure</h2>

  <p>My project investigates how exposure to psychoactive drugs during pregnancy, particularly opioids such as fentanyl and cannabis components such as Δ-9-THC, can affect fetal brain development and long-term behavior. Substance use during pregnancy is often complex, and many pregnancies affected by opioid exposure also involve exposure to other substances, including cannabis. However, we still know relatively little about how these drugs interact during development or how combined exposure may shape the fetal brain.</p>

